    <string name="category_flam">Flam rudiments</string>
    <string name="category_drag">Drag rudiments</string>
    <string name="tip_roll">Keep the strokes even: each hand should sound the same. For doubles, the second stroke must be as loud as the first, so use a little wrist on it instead of letting it bounce.</string>
    <string name="tip_diddle">The accent falls on the first note of each group and moves from hand to hand. Play the accent from a high stick and keep the taps low and relaxed.</string>
    <string name="tip_flam">A flam is a soft grace note just before the main stroke, from a low stick, with the other hand coming from high. Aim for a short \"flam\" sound, not two separate notes and not a flat single hit.</string>
    <string name="tip_drag">A drag is two quick, soft grace notes (a small double stroke) right before the main stroke. Keep them close to the head and close to the main note.</string>
